 egin{quote}\small  egin{enumerate}[label=(oman*), itemsep=1pt, topsep=2pt] \item ``below the fine grid the null truth carries MnvTune's [MINERvA Tune~v1's] shapes [as implemented, the Tune~v1 composition, varied by the drawn interaction-model universes, with every fine-cell integral held fixed at G's; \Sef{sec:joint5d-design}] and G's finite-MC fine-cell fluctuations: the [fine-grid convergence] check is not converged (fine vs merged-$	imes2$ is 0.50--0.86 of coarse vs fine in $L_{2}$); its effect enters the claim rule as the $\kappa=2$ variants and its size in null-$T$ units (with the frozen $V$) is committed before the first look'' \item ``the MC detector simulation per event beyond the drawn detector bands (MinosEfficiency, GEANT neutron/pion/proton, each $\pm1\sigma$) and the linear lateral surrogate (five bands); there is no recoil-energy-scale band in the analysis's systematic set [App.~ef{app:statmethods}], so hadronic-response completeness is not established'' \item ``the interaction-model prior is the analysis's vertical band set (34 bands, every band drawn per experiment); negative weights of LowQ2\_1/HighQ2\_1 are clipped per universe ([the effect of clipping rather than keeping them, measured on the pilot]: $\le0.35\%$ of a band's shift in whitened norm)'' \item ``the pseudo-experiment process unfolds with half the MC, the data with all of it; the MC-size shift $D$ (16 pairs) is at noise level per cell (median $|D|/f$ 0.02--0.075\%); along the null's bias direction it is not always consistent with zero (proxy $a/\mathrm{se}$ $+4.7$ MnvTune, $-3.4$ NuWro) but at most ${\sim}0.05$ null SD [measured with the frozen $V$ before any observed statistic: at most 0.068, the value used in (iv) below]; it enters as the bias-aligned upper-bound variant'' \item ``GiBUU: $E_{
u}>\SI{20}{GeV}$ absent [the GiBUU sample's energy limit, \Sef{sec:eavailw-band}] and its out-of-domain truth ($p_{\parallel}\ge\SI{6}{GeV/c}$, $E_{
u}$-truncated) enters the migrations into the domain cells; all generators: $E_{
u}>\SI{100}{GeV}$ absent (only the data's flux integral stops there; negligible)'' \item ``the predictions' own finite MC enters as $\mathrm{diag}\,\mathrm{Var}(\mu_{G})$ in the metric and as a drawn residual term'' \end{enumerate} \end{quote} 
